### 1. Architecture Overview

The codebase (Grafana repo, `knowledgeId: e0a5c5ee-310a-4bff-ab29-ef18eaab0826`) has **two distinct metrics middleware paths** for HTTP client instrumentation, both directly coupled to `prometheus.Registerer`:

**Path A — `PrometheusMetricsMiddleware` (generic HTTP client middleware)**
```
NewPrometheusMetricsMiddleware(prefix)
  → PrometheusMetrics{counter, failureCounter, histogram, gauge}
  → .Register(prometheus.Registerer) / .MustRegister() / .WithMustRegister()
  → PrometheusMetricsMiddleware(*PrometheusMetrics) → httpclient.Middleware
```

**Path B — `newMetricsMiddleware` / `NewMetricsMiddleware` (plugin client middleware)**
```
ProvideClientWithMiddlewares(... prometheus.Registerer ...)
  → CreateMiddlewares(... prometheus.Registerer ...)
    → clientmiddleware.NewMetricsMiddleware(promRegisterer, registry)
      → newMetricsMiddleware(promRegisterer, registry)
        → promRegisterer.MustRegister(5 prometheus collectors)
```

The refactor replaces `prometheus.Registerer` with a new `MetricsCollector` interface in both paths, so any component that registers HTTP client metrics through either middleware must implement that interface.

